[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one bug, one fix queued. Its reports say otherwise.
Read by body and placed by tenant, they hold three problems. One fix will not close them.

<Callout>
Not one issue. Three problems, each tracked on its own. The counts below are the desk's own view,
computed from the reports at render time, so they move when the desk merges more.
</Callout>

## The problems

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

| problem | counted in the table as | tracked in |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `parser` | the `parser` row | [issue #1](https://github.com/daniel-packard/what-it-shows/issues/1) |
| `hint` | the `hint` row | [issue #2](https://github.com/daniel-packard/what-it-shows/issues/2) |
| `one-day-move` | the one-day-move note: filed under `parser` by tenant, so also inside the `parser` row | [issue #3](https://github.com/daniel-packard/what-it-shows/issues/3) |

### `parser`: the shared parser reads dates month first

Day-first tenants write `07/04`, the parser reads 4 July. The day and month swap. This is the bug
#4471 was opened for, and most of its reports.

### `hint`: the booking-v3 form asks for the month first

booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type what the hint says, and the form
reads it the tenant's way, day first. Only reports sent through the booking-v3 form, from day-first
tenants. The parser fix does not touch it: the form needs its hint changed. Intake tags miss it both
ways, so place these reports by tenant and channel, not by tag.

### `one-day-move`: dates off by exactly one day

A flipped day and month cannot move a date by one day. These reports describe something else: the
same meeting on Tuesday in Lisbon and Monday in Toronto, every June booking a day off, an invite
that arrived before its booking. That points at time zones or daylight saving, not at date order.
The desk read them this way already. They stay counted where they are
filed, under `parser`, and are tracked on their own.

## How to place a new report

1. Read the body. A date off by one day is `one-day-move`; add its id to `desk-notes.json`.
2. Otherwise look up the tenant: reports through the booking-v3 form are `hint`.
3. Everything else from a day-first tenant is `parser`.

Do not merge on subject line alone ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)): all
three problems arrive under the same subjects.

